    "body": "## Background\n\nChunkPipe pretraining with a 512K sequence length and 8 chunks encounters OOM during the forward pass of the last chunk:\n\n```text\nFile \"megatron/core/transformer/multi_latent_attention.py\", line 564, in concat_cached_chunk_key_value_mla\n    mask_org = torch.ones(curr_len, total_concatenated_tokens, dtype=torch.bool,\ntorch.OutOfMemoryError: CUDA out of memory. Tried to allocate 32.00 GiB.\n```\n\n`concat_cached_chunk_key_value_mla` constructs a dense boolean mask of shape `[curr_len, total_concatenated_tokens]`. With a 512K sequence evenly divided into 8 chunks, the mask for the last chunk has a size of `65536 × 524288` bytes, requiring 32 GiB of GPU memory.\n\nHowever, in the non-DSA MLA pretraining path, `forward()` already switches `attn_mask_type` to `causal_bottom_right`, where the attention kernel handles causal masking internally. Therefore, explicitly constructing this dense mask is unnecessary.\n\n## Changes\n\nAdd a condition in `concat_cached_chunk_key_value_mla` to skip dense mask allocation when `causal_bottom_right` is used. The condition matches the one in `forward()`:\n\n```python\nuses_bottom_right = (\n    not self.config.sft_chunkpipe_mode\n    and self.config.experimental_attention_variant != \"dsa\"\n)\n\nif attention_mask is not None and not uses_bottom_right:\n    # Original mask construction logic remains unchanged.\n```\n\nWhen `uses_bottom_right` is true, `adjusted_mask` is set to `None`, avoiding the unnecessary allocation.\n\nThe existing behavior is preserved for SFT and DSA paths.\n\n## Scope and Impact\n\n- Affects only the non-DSA MLA path in ChunkPipe pretraining.\n- Eliminates the allocation of a dense mask of size `curr_len × total_concatenated_tokens` for each chunk forward pass.\n- Also benefits recomputation forward passes when activation recomputation is enabled.\n- Works with both uniform and non-uniform chunking. For example, with a 512K sequence split into 8 chunks, the first chunk has a length of 167040, and the original mask would require approximately 26 GiB. The new implementation reduces this allocation to zero.\n- SFT ChunkPipe, DSA, and non-ChunkPipe paths remain unchanged.",
